.TH EBPM 1 "2026-07-28" "ebasic 0.1.0" "eBasic Manual"
.SH NAME
ebpm \- the eBasic package manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ebpm
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.br
.B ebpm
.RB { \-v | \-\-version }
.br
.B ebpm
.RB { \-h | \-\-help }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ebpm
is a Cargo-style package manager for eBasic: a TOML manifest
(\fIebasic.toml\fR), path/git dependencies, and a lockfile
(\fIebasic.lock\fR) for reproducible builds.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI new " name"\fR\ [\-\-lib]
Scaffold a new package directory \fIname\fR/.
.TP
.BR init " [\-\-lib]"
Scaffold a package in the current directory.
.TP
.B build
Build the package in the current directory.
.TP
.BR run " [\-\- " args ...]
Build (if stale), then run the [bin] target. Arguments after a literal
\fB\-\-\fR are forwarded to the built program.
.TP
.B test
Build and run every \fItests/*.bas\fR file as a standalone program;
a test passes if its program exits 0.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ebc (1),
.BR docgen (1)
.br
Full documentation: <https://github.com/yann64/ebasic/blob/main/docs/guide/ebpm.md>
